{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJv15k4Zs3g1mM6rp7ZH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Matplotlib now has `matplotlib.__version_info__`, a named tuple like `sys.version_info` with the fields `(major, minor, micro, releaselevel, serial)`. That means checks like `matplotlib.__version_info__ >= (3, 4, 2)` compare correctly, even for versions like 3.10. The 4 tests in `test_matplotlib.py` pass, and I checked by hand that sample version strings parse as expected.\n\n**How it works** (in `lib/matplotlib/__init__.py`):\n- A new function `_parse_to_version_info` turns the version string into the tuple using `packaging`, which the module already imported.\n- I moved the existing version lookup into a helper, `_get_version()`. The first time you ask for either `__version__` or `__version_info__`, both are computed and saved.\n\n**How version strings become tuples:**\n\n| Version string | `releaselevel` | `serial` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `3.5.0` | `'final'` | 0 |\n| `3.5.0rc2` | `'candidate'` | 2 |\n| `3.5.1b1` | `'beta'` | 1 |\n| `3.5.0.dev820+g…` | `'alpha'` | 820 |\n| `3.5.0.post820+g…` | `'alpha'` | 820, and `micro` goes up by one (3.5.1) |\n\nThe last row is a guess that a post-release build leads to the next patch version. Because of it, this checkout (`0.0.post1+…`) reports `(0, 0, 1, 'alpha', 1)`.\n\nI also added a short release note at `doc/users/next_whats_new/version_info.rst`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":23489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384},"output_tokens":547,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dde9cf45-81db-4ba1-b630-b45ab4b26d7c","uuid":"ecd68cf3-1106-4fd4-9a9c-9a64913aefeb","timestamp":"2026-11-23T00:29:34.798Z","request_id":"req_011ChJv15cMyuJoXXgwUgije"}
